"2.1 - Information Storage"

  "Hexadecimal Notation"
  - Remember, since they are multiples of 16 (aka four binary bits), you  can "add" hex numbers together:

    0x17 = 0001 + 0111 = 00010111 = 23 (1*16 + 7*1)

  - You can convert from Hex back to Binary by splitting into groups of four bits the same way:

    0011 1100 1010 1101 1011 0011
     3    12   10   13   11   3
     0    C    A    D    B    3   0xCADB3

  - Remember, if there isn't a clean multiple of four, the padding goes on the left, always!

    1111 0010 1011 0110 1100 11 # WRONG!
    11 1100 1010 1101 1011 0011 # Correct 
